<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sultan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sultan is an Arabic title meaning authority or power, used by Muslim rulers. The Seljuk rulers were among the first to use it as a formal title, alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>. It was held by the rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a>, among others.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sultan.jpg" alt="Sultan" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Circle of Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EmperorSuleiman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
